      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(crestodian): suppress unhandled stdout/stderr stream errors in probeLocalCommand",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`probeLocalCommand` attaches `data` listeners to `child.stdout` and `child.stderr`, but does not attach `error` listeners. If either stream emits an `error` event, the unhandled error can crash the OpenClaw process.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdd no-op `error` handlers to both stdout and stderr streams after the data handlers. Stream read errors are treated as non-fatal because the child process `error`/`close` handlers already report the real outcome.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **`src/crestodian/probes.ts`** — add `child.stdout.on(\"error\", () => {})` and `child.stderr.on(\"error\", () => {})` (2 lines)\n\n## Evidence\n\nRegression test:\n\n```bash\nnode --import tsx/esm scripts/proof/probes-stream-errors.mts\n```\n\n```\n==============================================================\nProof: stream error handlers in probeLocalCommand\n==============================================================\n\nTest 1: Normal probeLocalCommand with a real command\n  found=true, version=v1.0.0, error=none\n  ✅ PASS: Normal probeLocalCommand still works after fix\n\nTest 2: Stream error on stdout does not crash\n  stdout received: \"version output\"\n  ✅ PASS: Process did not crash on stream error (handler suppressed it)\n\n==============================================================\n✅ PROOF PASSED — probeLocalCommand handles stream errors safely\n==============================================================\n```\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
        "branch": "fix/probes-stream-errors",
